## Build

The only requirement is an `arm-none-eabi` toolchain and `make`:

```bash
make            # -> build/{{TARGET}}.elf, .hex, .bin
make clean
```

On Fedora: `sudo dnf install arm-none-eabi-gcc-cs arm-none-eabi-newlib make`.
On Debian/Ubuntu: `sudo apt install gcc-arm-none-eabi make`.

## Flash

```bash
st-flash write build/{{TARGET}}.bin 0x8000000
# or
openocd -f interface/stlink.cfg -f target/stm32f4x.cfg \
  -c "program build/{{TARGET}}.elf verify reset exit"
```

## Layout

```
Core/Inc          headers, including the HAL configuration
Core/Src          main.c, interrupt handlers, low-level init
Core/Startup      ST's startup code for this part
Drivers           ST's HAL and CMSIS sources, copied in full
{{LDSCRIPT}}      memory map for this part
```

## Regenerating

Everything outside the `USER CODE BEGIN` / `USER CODE END` markers is
generated from the design plan and is overwritten when the project is
regenerated. Code inside the markers is preserved.

